From e5b71a8c0ae7ca0a03616ec0b0b7e5337f5beb64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:07:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] emacs_options: keyword constants, plist keys, inline
 repeats, choices and function names as Customize takes them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bridge reads a keyword at the end of a type as its argument (`(const :utf-8)`), makes a property list's keys keywords whatever its key type (`(symbol :tag …)`, a choice of keywords), gives an inline repeat of a list the rest of its items (org-latex-classes with sectioning), picks a choice's alternative by what the value names (a constant's name, a list that starts with one, a string where strings are taken), and takes a function's name for a function. A value left out names the item that does not fit. The editor's emacs_options goes over the file's option by option, `[]` keeping the file's; a TOML date is its text. The options page records docstrings with Org loaded, functions as written and versions as `Org 9.8`; VS Code's example of org-lsp.settings uses the current names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
