From 54d18ebb238e69c7e0438bfc9920e6183eba6d05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:38:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Commands through Emacs say what Emacs says, and Emacs
 holds up the server less
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What Emacs says last is shown after the command's edit too (C-c C-a a's "File … is now an attachment"), and a code block that fails shows Babel's error output (stderr, exit code) as a warning. C-c C-a u asks in the editor about a download Org does not consider safe, and org_resource_download_policy and org_safe_remote_resources reach Emacs; the dispatcher has q and says "No such attachment command: x". A second countdown asks "Replace current timer?" and takes the answer; commands run with this-command bound (org-plot/gnuplot's message). A diary sexp that fails says Org's "Bad sexp at line N in FILE: …" once. Notices of emacs_options are shown once in a session, and an Emacs that stops says its exit status.

A request that waits for Emacs waits for its start 15 s at most and behind another job 3 s, and says which it was; one that is late names what Emacs was asked. The server stops its Emacs and what Emacs started when it exits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
