From c588335ee4e08e9c9b596a8871f1ee1956507f6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:07:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Commands that wait for Emacs hold up no other answer, and
 can be canceled
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A command the editor asks for that needs Emacs's answer (the export menu, a capture template's %(…) and target function, org-edit-special, the attachments to pick, refile targets a function verifies, the countdown's default, the named blocks, the structure templates, org-agenda-to-appt, a heading made of a region) sends Emacs the job and is answered once Emacs has answered: the server answers the other requests meanwhile, and runs the command again from the start with Emacs's answer at hand. $/cancelRequest gives such a request up, and stops Emacs if it works on it (a %(…) that loops); the next request starts it again. What is not a command (the agenda's diary sexps and prefixes, image previews, org-crypt before a save) still waits, as protocol.org says.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
