index 6d576e4..003fdbe 100644
--- a/docs/protocol.org
+++ b/docs/protocol.org
@@ -2063,18 +2063,33 @@ export never holds up the server's other answers. Emacs loads, in this
 order, ~emacs_config_file~, then evaluates ~emacs_config~, then loads Org
 (~org~, ~ox~, ~ox-publish~): settings made before Org loads are kept
 (~org-export-backends~ to add Markdown, a ~load-path~ for another Org), and
-the configuration may load Org itself. A request whose answer is Emacs's
-(the export menu, a capture template's ~%(…)~, a diary sexp, an agenda
-prefix's ~%(…)~, the attachments to pick) waits for it, and holds up the
-server's other answers meanwhile. It has a time of its own (10 to 120
-seconds), past which Emacs is taken for stuck and started again (/Emacs
-did not answer in time: `eval` took over 30 s …/); the time Emacs takes
-to start is not counted in it, but waited for 15 seconds at most (/Emacs
-is still starting …/, and Emacs goes on starting for the next request),
